    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Summary\nWindows installers ship entirely unsigned, so Defender SmartScreen shows \"unknown publisher\" on first run and keeps warning until reputation accrues (slow-to-never for unsigned binaries). At 10k users this is a large first-run drop-off.\n\n## Root cause\n`frontend/makers/maker-nsis.ts:39-80` has no `certificateFile`/`signtool`/Azure Trusted Signing/sign hook, and neither CI workflow carries Windows signing secrets. Target is NSIS only.\n\n## Expected\nSign the Windows installer (EV certificate or Azure Trusted Signing).\n\n## Suggested fix\nAdd Windows code signing to the NSIS maker plus the release workflow. Bulk of the effort is certificate procurement.\n\n## Notes\nUNTESTED (needs Windows first-run); verified from config. QA audit finding INST-2. Effort: days (mostly procurement). Scaling risk: critical.\n",
